	// If any error occurs, we should not output partial? Or we output? For earlier case with second line leading spaces, we output partial? Let's see: For U TEST "json.a = 1;\n  json.b = 2;\n" second line leading two spaces, it gave output only first (a:1), no error. So it ignored second line (because leading spaces). So no error.

	// For "json.a = 1;\n\tjson.b = 2;\n" second line leading tab, it gave error "ungron failed for ``: invalid statement" and no output (exit 5). So tab leading second line causes error abort.

	// For "json.a = 1;\n\njson.b = 2;\n" blank line between, it gave both a and b, no error.

