			} else {
				// Should not happen for json stream? In gron json stream, object values are only empty object markers, not full objects. But just in case, treat as object with values? Actually for ungron merging, if value is non-empty object, would be unusual. We'll treat as empty object? Let's attempt to convert to ordered map? But for simplicity, treat non-empty map as something that would cause merge? In original, json stream never has non-empty object as value, only {}.
