	// Let's check remaining: we can get the offset by using dec.InputOffset? Not available in older Go. We can approximate by trying to see if trimmedValue after removing prefix of marshaled value still has non-space.

	// For "truex", trimmedValue = "truex", v=true, marshaled "true", remaining "x" -> should error for non-number

	// For "1x", v would be number 1 if we use number prefix extraction, but if we use json.Decoder, it would decode 1 and leave "x" as extra, but we want to allow for numbers.

